<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union of Arms</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1626</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union of Arms was a plan put forward by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspar-de-guzman-count-duke-of-olivares">Count-Duke of Olivares</a> in 1626 for every kingdom of the Spanish monarchy to supply a fixed reserve of paid soldiers for common defence. Resisted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-courts">Catalan Courts</a> and other realms, it fed the grievances that led to the revolts of Catalonia and Portugal in 1640.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/union-of-arms.jpg" alt="Union of Arms" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nagihuin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uni%C3%B3n_de_Armas.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
